<newsitem itemid="658899" id="root" date="1997-06-13" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Lenco shows strong year earnings recovery.</title>
<headline>Lenco shows strong year earnings recovery.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - before except.	46.3	  vs 34.6</p>
<p>    - after except.	 41.6	  vs loss 28.0</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 20.0	  vs 19.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   32.93	 vs loss 22.12</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   42.21	 vs loss 11.02</p>
<p>    Tax			 10.92	 vs 10.67</p>
<p>    Interest paid	    9.84	 vs 14.35</p>
<p>    Turnover		 667.78	 vs 727.48</p>
<p>    Exceptionals  paid     3.59	 vs 49.49</p>
<p>Div payable July 7</p>
<p>on register June 27</p>
<p>Full name: Lenco Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Directors said that they were confident that the group would continue to show recovered growth in the current year after a realignment of its operations.</p>
<p>It saud it should also finalise negotiations currently underway -- which led to a cautionary announcement on May 20 -- by the end of June.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
